bibliograph-worker (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.6 release: lockstep version bump, no worker payload changes.

    - The admin edition editor writes the catalog through the web pool; the
      existing catalog triggers queue the edition and entity records for
      pds-publish, so the worker and its publication path are unchanged.
    - The catalog schema is unchanged (0001-0004 are still the current
      files); this release applies no migration.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.5 release: cleanup of retired tooling and dead compatibility code.

    - Drop the unreachable record-field fallbacks in the edition builders:
      series values are objects only, and contributor displayName and
      name_inverted no longer probe the retired books-wg spellings.
    - Remove an unused admin body helper and the re-exported metrics
      constants; behaviour of the admin API and the metrics listener is
      unchanged.
    - Delete the retired combined-package build tree (root `debian/`) and its
      five mise tasks from the source; the split packages and deploy flow are
      unchanged.
    - Retire stale environment variables (pool overrides, labeler keys, cover
      cache, legacy rate limits) and align `.env.example` and the docs with
      the current deployment.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:20:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.4 release: OpenLibrary provider and admin contributor search.

    - Add an OpenLibrary provider (search, ISBN and OL key/edition lookups,
      edition and author parsing) behind the shared retry/breaker/metrics
      wrapper.
    - Make OpenLibrary the final hydration fallback, so the order is
      ISBNdb -> Google Books -> Goodreads -> OpenLibrary; an empty or failing
      provider still falls through, and the first error is rethrown only when
      every step is empty.
    - Accept `openlibrary` in the worker admin /provider-search endpoint,
      including ISBN and OL key queries, and add /contributor-search backed
      by OpenLibrary author documents.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:20:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.3 release: contributor/publisher records and entity preparation.

    - Build and publish net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.contributor and
      .publisher records (strict YYYY-MM-DD dates, defs#identifier
      identifiers, optional image and blob), and dispatch pds_outbox rows
      by collection instead of assuming editions.
    - Mint contributor/publisher at-URIs at ingest and link edition snapshots
      to them through defs#contributor.ref / defs#publisher.ref.
    - Ship the additive, idempotent 0004-entity-records.sql schema: at_uri
      and metadata columns, partial unique URI indexes, identifier GIN
      indexes and snapshot triggers. It queues nothing on its own.
    - Add the idempotent entities.prepare task and `--prepare-entities` CLI
      to mint URIs, enqueue entity records and republish linked editions.
    - Scope the outbox backlog metrics to the published collection
      allowlist.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.2 release: PDS session refresh and metrics.

    - Refresh the publisher PDS session when a call is rejected with 400
      ExpiredToken, then retry the write once, so queued pds_outbox rows keep
      draining after an access token expires.
    - Expose bibliograph_worker_up, the pds_outbox ready/parked/oldest-age
      backlog gauges and per-scrape process gauges on the existing loopback
      /metrics listener.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.1 release: lexicon.community PR #18 edition records.

    - Build published edition records with contributors[].displayName and
      ONIX role codes (normalized; default A01) from the imported PR #18
      defs lexicon, replacing the legacy name/author fields.
    - Republish existing editions through pds_outbox so PDS records match the
      new contributor shape without changing URIs.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.0 release: catalog reliability and curation.

    - Retry provider calls with per-provider circuit breakers, and expose the
      breaker state and ISBNdb daily usage on the metrics listener.
    - Enforce the daily ISBNdb quota before a request is made, and reject
      ISBNdb calls while its breaker is open.
    - Add the authenticated admin API (ADMIN_TOKEN) for provider search,
      publisher search, publisher book preview and bounded bulk import.
    - Keep ISBNdb citation and synopsis text intact while unwrapping.
    - Ship the versioned catalog schema (0001-0003) inside the package.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. The graphile-worker from packages/worker, with its
    production dependencies deployed beside it:

    - catalog.resolve / catalog.search hydrate the catalog from Google Books,
      ISBNdb and Goodreads;
    - pds-publish drains public.pds_outbox into the publisher PDS with
      com.atproto.repo.applyWrites, choosing create/update from pds_cids and
      recording the returned CID;
    - /etc/bibliograph/worker.env carries the database URL, publisher identity
      and optional provider keys.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
